\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Fix site dimension $q\geq 2$ and bounds $J,Delta>0$. For every L-by-L square-grid Hamiltonian with site and nearest-neighbor terms of norm at most J, a unique normalized ground vector and global spectral gap at least Delta, does there exist a PEPS of maximum bond dimension at most C $L^c$ whose normalized vector is within $L^{-1}$, up to global phase, of that ground vector, with C,c depending only on q,J,Delta?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Fix site dimension $q\geq 2$ and bounds $J,Delta>0$. For every L-by-L square-grid Hamiltonian with site and nearest-neighbor terms of norm at most J, a unique normalized ground vector and global spectral gap at least Delta, does there exist a PEPS of maximum bond dimension at most C $L^c$ whose normalized vector is within $L^{-1}$, up to global phase, of that ground vector, with C,c depending only on q,J,Delta?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Polynomial-PEPS-approximation-of-gapped-square-grid-ground-states-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex}.
